      "title": "START HERE",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Open-H3 Regenerate 2K — Draft Video\nRegenerates a **low-resolution draft** (an H3 768P render, or a 384P–576P clip from LTX, Wan, SANA-Video…) **natively at 2560×1440** (or 768P / 1080P / 4K) with NVIDIA's open replacement for the closed H3-Regenerate-2K API ([project page](https://nvlabs.github.io/Sana/Open-H3-Regenerate-2K/)). Content, layout and motion come from the draft; the 3 refine steps redraw faces, fabric, fur and foliage at full size.\n\n## Use\n1. **Load the draft** in *Draft video* (24 fps is used as is, other rates are resampled).\n2. **Prompt** — written automatically: *Video to H3 Prompt* sends the prepared draft to your OpenAI-compatible vision server (set `server_url`; API key from the environment variable named in `api_key_env`, default `H3_LLM_API_KEY`) and feeds the result to the encoder; check it in *Generated H3 prompt*. To use your own prompt instead (e.g. the one the H3 draft was made with), paste it into the node's `manual_prompt`.\n3. **Run.** Output: `output/video/open_h3_regen_2k_*.mp4` with the draft's own soundtrack.\n\n## Settings (reference recipe — leave as is)\n* *Prepare Draft* `size` **768p** for H3 drafts, **576p** for drafts from other models; `max_frames` 121 = 5 s (5–15 s / up to 360 frames work in one pass, much slower).\n* *Latent Upscale* `resolution` **2k**; 1080p computes 1920×1088 and crops to 1080; **4k** runs the upscaler twice (via 2K).\n* *Sigmas* `steps` **3** (σ 0.909 → 0.857 → 0.667 → 0). `steps` 2 is ~30 % faster but softer on fur / moss. `start_sigma` 0.8 = gentler (the project page's 768P → 4K ladder).\n* Sampler **euler**, **CFG 1** (Basic Guider), seed fixed. The LoRA node applies the merged refiner + LightX2V Turbo + LMS Sharp LoRA and the 50 Sharp curve branches (curve table from `minimax_h3_ref2va_pruned_int8_convrot`).\n* Audio is held as encoded silence while refining (reference); the final MP4 gets the draft's soundtrack.\n* **Fast H3 VAE decoder** (NVIDIA StreamRender-H3, 24 layers): 22 s instead of 50 s at 2K. To use ComfyUI's own decoder instead, replace it with a *VAE Decode* fed by *Video VAE*.\n* **Sol-Attn sparse attention is on** (SoL-Engine's biggest speed-up): all 3 steps sparse, 3.9× faster here with the same look. Select it and press Ctrl+B for dense attention.\n* **Identity drifting?** σ 0.909 redraws a lot: in tests a small fox face drifted towards a wolf (darker coat, lost ear tips) while layout and motion held. Set *Sigmas* `start_sigma` **0.8** (the project page's own 4K ladder setting) to stay closer to the draft; 0.7 is gentler still.\n\n## Models\nFL2VA pruned int8 (`minimax_h3_fl2va_pruned_int8_convrot`, the reference base is FL2VA) · `H3/Open-H3-Regenerate-2K/` LoRA (12.4 GB) + curve branches · LBH `minimax_h3_latent_upscaler_3d_conv_v1` · H3 video/audio VAE · Qwen3-VL 32B encoder.\n\n**Needs:** ComfyUI-Open-H3-Regenerate · Comfyui_Minimax_h3_latent_Upscaler (LBH).\n\n**Time:** measured on the RTX PRO 5000, 5 s clip (121 frames) at **2K ≈ 3 min** warm: 3 refine steps ≈ 122 s with Sol-Attn (474 s dense), fast VAE decode ≈ 24 s (native 50 s), encode / upscale / save ≈ 30 s. A cold start measured 206 s in total. 15 s clips and 4K cost several times more — try 5 s first."
      ],
      "color": "#2a2a2a",
      "bgcolor": "#353535"
    },
